 ### [PointSplat](14667-pointsplat.md)
-PointSplat is a geometry-driven prune-and-refine framework for 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) that enables high-quality reconstruction of compact Gaussian sets without requiring per-scene optimization at deployment. It bridges the gap between Gaussian pruning and transformer refinement by using intrinsic 3D attributes for pruning and a dual-branch encoder for refinement. Unlike image-driven pruning methods (e.g., LightGaussians, PUP-3DGS, Speedy-Splat) that rely on 2D images and per-scene optimization, PointSplat uses only 3D attributes for pruning. Unlike SplatFormer, which concatenates all Gaussian parameters into a single feature vector causing appearance dominance due to high-dimensional spherical harmonics, PointSplat decouples geometry and appearance.
+PointSplat is a geometry-driven prune-and-refine framework for 3D Gaussian Splatting that enables high-quality reconstruction of compact Gaussian sets without requiring per-scene optimization at deployment. It bridges the gap between Gaussian pruning and transformer refinement by using intrinsic 3D attributes for pruning and a dual-branch encoder for refinement. Unlike image-driven pruning methods that rely on 2D images and per-scene optimization, PointSplat uses only 3D attributes for pruning. Unlike SplatFormer, which concatenates all Gaussian parameters into a single feature vector causing appearance dominance due to high-dimensional spherical harmonics, PointSplat decouples geometry and appearance.
+
+### [Full Factors Weighted (FFW) Importance Score Pruning](19837-full-factors-weighted-ffw-importance-score-pruning.md)
+FFW computes an importance score for each Gaussian primitive using a combination of position, color, opacity, and transparency to selectively remove less important Gaussians while preserving visual quality. It is chosen when explicit multi-factor weighting is preferred over normalized z-score aggregation [G].
 
